# --- Server ---
PORT=4000
NODE_ENV=development
# Comma-separated list is not needed; single origin of your deployed/local frontend
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Database ---
# Hosted Postgres connection string (Neon/Supabase/Render Postgres/etc). Include ?sslmode=require in production.
# On a serverless/pooled Postgres (Neon, etc.), also add &connection_limit=5&pool_timeout=20 —
# without it Prisma defaults to (CPU cores * 2 + 1) connections per instance, which can exhaust a
# free-tier pooled connection budget surprisingly fast, especially across frequent dev-server
# restarts. See https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm/prisma-client/setup-and-configuration/databases-connections/connection-pool
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/razorrecover?connection_limit=5&pool_timeout=20

# --- Razorpay Test Mode ---
# No longer an env var: each merchant connects their own Razorpay Test Mode account from inside
# the app (Policies & Audit → Razorpay Connection, after logging in) — see routes/merchant.ts.
# A payment-recovery tool only has anything to recover on the account whose checkout actually
# failed, so a single app-wide credential stopped making sense once there was more than one real
# merchant. Simulations don't need this at all; only live webhooks and real retries/payment links do.

# --- AI reasoning layer ---
# If unset, the AI layer reports "unavailable" and ambiguous cases route straight to human
# review — a safe, expected fallback, not an error.
#
# Uses Groq (https://console.groq.com — free, no card required) by default. GROQ_BASE_URL only
# needs to change if you want to point at a *different* OpenAI-compatible provider instead (e.g.
# Gemini's compatibility layer: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/, model
# gemini-2.0-flash) — no code changes either way, since they all speak the same chat-completions
# + tool-calling API this app's AI layer already uses.
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
GROQ_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1

# --- Session ---
# Any long random string; signs the mock merchant session cookie
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
